# Pairs with RecoverNeverInsideCommitted. The pre-#5810 phase-2 commit on the
# successor: no fence, and a blind TAIL upsert from the successor's own highest
# commit. A predecessor's late batch commits above the successor's recovered
# allocator; the successor's next commit regresses TAIL beneath it, and the
# next re-seed, which reads TAIL alone, hands out an offset a committed batch
# holds: the regression escalates to a reissue.
MODULE: RecoverNeverInsideCommittedUnfencedBlindTail
TARGET: RecoverNeverInsideCommitted
CLASS: Action
SUMMARY: a successor's unfenced commit regresses TAIL and the next re-seed lands inside a committed batch
PERTURBS: FlushAck

--- FIND
       IF /\ ~WithCrossSiloMove \/ curFresh
          /\ occ[o] = "none" \/ (kind = "ackedMid" /\ occ[o] = "latePrev")
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: the successor's commit is not conditional on its view of TAIL.
       IF /\ occ[o] = "none" \/ (kind = "ackedMid" /\ occ[o] = "latePrev")
--- END

--- FIND
            /\ ct' = IF WithCrossSiloMove THEN Max({ct, o}) ELSE ct
            /\ UNCHANGED curFresh
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: TAIL is upserted from the successor's own highest commit.
            /\ ct' = IF WithCrossSiloMove
                     THEN Max({p \in Offs : occ[p] \in {"acked", "ackedMid", "late", "dup"}} \cup {-1, o})
                     ELSE ct
            /\ UNCHANGED curFresh
--- END
--- FIND
WithCrossSiloMove == FALSE
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: raises the bound so a lost activation may move to another silo.
WithCrossSiloMove == TRUE
--- END
